{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/862831-on-the-origin-of-the-dragonblood-exaltation-an-overview-of-an-immaculate-dispute","id":862831,"title":"On the origin of the Dragonblood Exaltation. An overview of an Immaculate dispute.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-09T16:28:07-07:00","id":862831,"title":"On the origin of the Dragonblood Exaltation. An overview of an Immaculate dispute.","content":"So, I have not visited this forum in... a year and a half? That's long. I guess it is high time I post something again. Immaculate theology sounds fun? It does.<br /> <br /> . <div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Question of Origination - an overview.</span></span></span></span></b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201cThe Question of Origination\u201d as it came to be called is perhaps the single most known theological dispute to have taken place within the Immaculate Religion. It should come as no surprise that it concerns the most important state for the followers of this religion: the Dragonblooded Exaltation. Although in modern days it is often considered an irrelevant speculation, rendered down to seemingly minute and trite question of \u201cis the Exaltation </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>of</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> the Dragons or </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>from </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">the Dragons\u201d and humorously referred to as \u201cthe Question of Preposition\u201d (a term made famous by a satirist and libertine Ragara Kamoka in RY 623), the impact of this divide is hard to overstate when it comes to contemporary Immaculate theology.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ever since the seminal works of Mnemon Avako, it had come to be widely accepted that the Question of Origination is almost as old as the Immaculate Religion itself, and dates back to first, failed attempts at establishing a canon of Immaculate Texts in the early days of the Shogunate. The writings contained in the corpus of works that would later form what is now the most common canon of the Texts tended to refer to the Exaltation of the Dragonbloods as coming \u201cfrom\u201d the Dragons. However, that was not universal, and some of them \u2013 namely \u201cThe Song of Five Elements\u201d, \u201cSecond Lamentation of Mela\u201d and all of the Hymns of Fire \u2013 instead used the formula of the \u201cExaltation of the Dragons born\u201d. Although at first ignored \u2013 or simply glossed over \u2013 the inconsistency quickly became apparent among the sages of the era. Traditionally, it is claimed that the first monk to take note of this was a woman named Lia, hailing from still-functioning Kasang Monastery in the eastern Blessed Island. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Supposedly, she declared before the abbot of the monastery that she uncovered proof of the bulk of Immaculate Texts being either incomplete or tampered with, citing the inconsistency which would later become the Question as a proof.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It is difficult to verify this story, and many scholars have attempted to declare it a simple legend \u2013 especially since there are no solid sources from that epoch that would prove the existence of monk named Lia. On the other hand, the monastery had been burnt down during the times of the Contagion, and much of its records lost. Furthermore, there actually is a lot of solid evidence which would indicate that it was in that region that the debates around the Question first gained wider attention.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At any rate, the debates spread through the monasteries and centers of learning of the Immaculate Religion, and quickly created a pointed division. At one side \u2013 known as \u201cthe traditionalists\u201d \u2013 the inconsistency in the texts was declared to be a simple case of erroneous translation, and the more common phrase \u2013 \u201cfrom the Dragons\u201d was proper. The other, far less popular opinion \u2013 \u201cthe Essentialists\u201d as they came to be called later \u2013 instead claimed that the existence of the phrase \u201cfrom the Dragons\u201d was a result of the texts being tampered with, and \u201cof the Dragons\u201d was the proper form. Their main argument, admittedly shaky, was based on the fact that the works in which the phrase \u201cof the Dragons\u201d was present were, at that time, considered some of the oldest, if the oldest parts of the Immaculate Canon.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">What needs to be said straight out was that this question did not concern a trivial matter with no bearing on how the Religion actually operated. The opposite was the case. The Question of Origination had far-reaching implications for interpretations of several core tenants of the Immaculate Religion.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The traditionalist stance \u2013 considered orthodox to this day \u2013 mandated that the Exaltation, as passed from the Dragons, is a form of a blessing offered and given by some distinct force. This in turn led to the relevance of doctrines ascribing the Immaculate Dragons with concrete existence and often agency and sentience. Furthermore, by presenting the Exaltation as a kind of a blessing, it reinforced the belief that the Dragonbloods are just </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>exalted</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> and elevated far above the common men, but not divine in their substance. In a way, it helped to bridge the rift between mortal and Exalted members of the faith, by presenting the latter as just significantly more perfect, instead of being fundamentally different and separate.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Essentialists on the other hand, with their view of the Exaltation being \u201cof the Dragons\u201d believed \u2013 as far a singular belief can be ascribed to this notoriously amorphous movement \u2013 that the Exaltation into being a Dragonblood means a form of consubstantiation with the Dragons, often understood more as cosmic principles rather than sentient agents. This, in turn, meant that the Dragonbloods are, at least partially, perfect and divine not by proximity to some sort of an ideal that blesses them as a reward for that, but rather because of their very nature, which actively participates in cosmic perfection. This conclusion often led to two more beliefs characteristic for most Essentialists. First, that as beings in part divine, they were not only destined to rule Creation, but also were the only actual agents of divinity in Creation and Heavens, and spirits \u2013 including gods \u2013 were supposed to be servants, and any sort of veneration for them was blasphemous, while offering worship to the Dragonbloods could be considered proper. Second, a Dragonblood, perfect by their very nature, could not act against the principles of the Immaculate Religion, and if a Dragonblood did just that \u2013 for example, by not following the Immaculate Faith \u2013 then he was no real Dragonblood, but instead an imposter, one of the Anathema. The consequences of such a categorization should not need to be explained.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It should come as no surprise that the Essentialist view swiftly became associated with the most radical and often openly heretical sects within the Immaculate Religion, and Essentialism grew to be a byword for all forms of extreme religious fundamentalism coming from the followers of this faith. However, while today the word may have lost much of its meaning and became something of a catch-all term for all manners of Immaculate fanaticism (no longer than in RY 743, Peleps Karada gained an Essentialist reputation for his zealotry in rooting out unsanctioned cults in the Threshold, while himself having several times admitted to a very traditionalist view), it needs to be said straight away that not every Essentialist was a radical or a fundamentalist. Although usually considered heterodoxical at best, if not outright heretical, this view in itself had never been openly and officially condemned by the authorities of the Immaculate Religion. In fact, some of the best known and best regarded officials of the faith were Essentialists.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">We should look no further for an example than to an important Essentialist thinker and poet Cynis Kazu, who ascended to the position of the Mouth of Peace in RY 345, and subsequently gained the moniker \u201cthe Just\u201d. His belief in the inherent perfection of the Dragonbloods gave him the conviction to strive for perfection in every aspect of his life, and encourage that in others, while accepting no sort of moral failings or corruption among the ranks of the Immaculates. Today, he is remembered for calling the Wyld Hunt on his own cousin, Cynis Redia, an abbess of a monastery in the Three Leaves Satrapy, infamous for her depravity and corruption.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This does not prevent the Essentialism for having a bad reputation both within and without the Immaculate Religion. Usually represented by the zealots of the worst kind, and extremely insular in its pursuit of perfection, it was never interested in gaining more formal recognition, or widening its reach. Today, about one in fifteen Immaculates espouses views which can be considered Essentialist, although this statistic rises to as high as one in five when it comes to the veterans of the Wyld Hunt, and one in three among the monks from the Kasang Monastery.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Postscript</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Although the above overview refers to the Essentialism in a way that would suggest it to be a distinct movement, it cannot be stressed enough that there is no single Essentialist school, and in fact the term itself is more of an awkward label than an accurate descriptor. For example, although both Kazuists and Guseists are considered Essentialists in their beliefs, suggesting any sort of a closeness of views between the two groups is a good way to become a public enemy of the family of Cynis Kazu.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1597,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1597-gargulec","user":"Gargulec","date":". 04-09-2016, 08:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":19}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1597-gargulec","name":"Gargulec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T18:47:15-07:00","id":862939,"title":"","content":"This feels like a very plausible in-setting academic piece. I feel like I could actually use it as-is and be satisfied with it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T18:55:46-07:00","id":862944,"title":"","content":"It's nicely written. The explanation of the opposing stances and the historical anecdotes throughout are great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 04-09-2016, 10:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T19:20:07-07:00","id":862958,"title":"","content":"Seems i portray my characters as generally Essentialists. Thank you for the interesting read!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T19:43:27-07:00","id":862968,"title":"","content":"I dunno, expanding on &quot;of vs. from&quot; into &quot;the single most known theological dispute&quot; seems, to me, a lot like the Expanded Universe inflating single throwaway lines about things like parsecs in the Kessel Run from an obvious attempt by a criminal to bamboozle what he thought were just some yokels into a factual truth on the matter of the route one is willing to fly through the gravity well of a cluster of black holes. <br /> <br /> Plus, there are plenty of other theological disputes between Immaculates. Faith vs. Philosophy, for instance, or that version practiced in the Dreaming Sea, where Dragon-Blooded are literally worshipped as gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-10-2016, 08:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T20:27:38-07:00","id":862983,"title":"","content":"Peleps Deled disapproves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T20:41:22-07:00","id":862985,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but he's a crazy murder-happy asshole, so who cares?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T21:50:48-07:00","id":863009,"title":"","content":"Gaaaaargawargawarga!<br /> <br /> This is excellent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/862831-on-the-origin-of-the-dragonblood-exaltation-an-overview-of-an-immaculate-dispute?p=862968#post862968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, expanding on &quot;of vs. from&quot; into &quot;the single most known theological dispute&quot; seems, to me, a lot like the Expanded Universe inflating single throwaway lines about things like parsecs in the Kessel Run from an obvious attempt by a criminal to bamboozle what he thought were just some yokels into a factual truth on the matter of how close one is willing to fly through the gravitational pulls of a cluster of black holes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like an academic expounding upon a question would use that sort of language whether it was true or not!<br /> <br /> I mean, goodness knows I've read enough papers declaring everything from grain tariffs to ludonarrative dissonance to be the Most Important Thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","user":"Guancyto","date":". 04-10-2016, 12:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T21:58:26-07:00","id":863012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/862831-on-the-origin-of-the-dragonblood-exaltation-an-overview-of-an-immaculate-dispute?p=862985#post862985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but he's a crazy murder-happy asshole, so who cares?</div> </div> </div> </div>... anyone that doesn't want to get killed for suggesting something might be correct and not in agreement with the view of Deled?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T23:26:30-07:00","id":863044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/862831-on-the-origin-of-the-dragonblood-exaltation-an-overview-of-an-immaculate-dispute?p=862968#post862968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, expanding on &quot;of vs. from&quot; into &quot;the single most known theological dispute&quot; seems, to me, a lot like the Expanded Universe inflating single throwaway lines about things like parsecs in the Kessel Run from an obvious attempt by a criminal to bamboozle what he thought were just some yokels into a factual truth on the matter of how close one is willing to fly through the gravitational pulls of a cluster of black holes.<br /> <br /> Plus, there are plenty of other theological disputes between Immaculates. Faith vs. Philosophy, for instance, or that version practiced in the Dreaming Sea, where Dragon-Blooded are literally worshipped as gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's fine. Essentially, we have very little info on theological arguments <i>within</i> the Immaculate Philosophy. And I find that in DB games, certain players (not all, but some) want to be able to argue about the theology of their extremely important religion. Not against Lookshy's Immaculate Faith: that's obviously wrong! No need for dynasts to argue about it.<br /> <br /> So, since you want to make up some theological arguments, you might as well base them on bits we know. It's not that big a deal. Were the writers making up some, of course, they could make up something completely new. But for us fans, I think it helps to extrapolate. Makes it feel that your own stuff is more part of the game.<br /> (Of course, I can see the point that maybe Pelleps Delled was supposed to be arguing about something very small that most Monks wouldn't care about, not a major theological argument)<br /> <br /> And writing long tracts about single lines is very, very appropriate for theological arguments.<br /> <br /> I like this document: the arguments about the nature of Dragonblood remind me very much about 4th-6th century arguments about Jesus' nature (one human and one divine nature that are seperate? One nature both divine and human? One human and one divine nature mixed together? A divine nature that subsumes his human nature?). These rested on a very small number of Biblical lines (such as &quot;Because humans are men of flesh and blood, Christ became like a human&quot;), but were mostly argued because of their theological ramifications (if Jesus has a divine and human nature, could the human half sin? Could it say things that are wrong? If his human nature is subsumed by his divine nature, can we say Jesus is a human at all?). Like how this is arguing about the theological ramifications of from vs of (for example, if DBs are of the Dragons, this means they are fundamentally different from humans).<br /> <br /> Incidentally, in my friend's game, the devision between &quot;of&quot; and &quot;from&quot; the dragons was known as &quot;oranges and apples&quot; because at one point Monks had a huge argument about whether legionaries should be supplied with oranges or apples.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-10-2016, 02:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T23:37:15-07:00","id":863047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guancyto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/862831-on-the-origin-of-the-dragonblood-exaltation-an-overview-of-an-immaculate-dispute?p=863009#post863009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, goodness knows I've read enough papers declaring everything from grain tariffs to ludonarrative dissonance to be the Most Important Thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>In defense of those people, when you spend forty years of your life researching, experimenting and unraveling the mysteries behind bee mating habits, it can FEEL like they're the most important thing in the entire world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T23:41:08-07:00","id":863048,"title":"","content":"Oh yes, this one is definitely reminiscent of the old Arian vs Nicean conflict in the early Christian Church during the Roman Empire. Its was over something as simple as 'Is Jesus a creation of God, divine but separate, or is Jesus God in mortal flesh?' People killed over it, and emperors took sides on the issue. The Niceans won out as far as the Catholic and Orthodox are concerned, but the divide hasn't truly disappeared - it's just that fewer people care about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T00:04:40-07:00","id":863052,"title":"","content":"Often these things take on a political dimension: the Goths weren't keen on joining the Roman church, they wanted their own form of Christianity, hence why Arianism did well amongst them.<br /> <br /> Similarly, I could see different houses supporting different monks or theological schools, so that they can lord it over the other houses.<br /> After all, in a place as big as the Realm, I imagine there is some variance in religion.<br /> Perhaps something like the different schools of Tibetan Buddhism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T00:10:40-07:00","id":863055,"title":"","content":"This is an interesting thing. I like it, and think we ought to encourage similar things. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>All that I write but don't cite is simply my perspective, colored by my experiences and beliefs. I extrapolate a lot, too, so don't take it too seriously. :P","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7858-end","name":"*End","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7858_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T03:44:21-07:00","id":863097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/862831-on-the-origin-of-the-dragonblood-exaltation-an-overview-of-an-immaculate-dispute?p=862968#post862968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, expanding on &quot;of vs. from&quot; into &quot;the single most known theological dispute&quot; seems, to me, a lot like the Expanded Universe inflating single throwaway lines about things like parsecs in the Kessel Run from an obvious attempt by a criminal to bamboozle what he thought were just some yokels into a factual truth on the matter of how close one is willing to fly through the gravitational pulls of a cluster of black holes.<br /> <br /> Plus, there are plenty of other theological disputes between Immaculates. Faith vs. Philosophy, for instance, or that version practiced in the Dreaming Sea, where Dragon-Blooded are literally worshipped as gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>The late antiquity christological debates, which have caused some of the most far-reaching divides within the body of Christianity could be rendered to disputing a difference whether Christ should be referred to as <i>homoio\u00fasios or homoousios. This debate was, among others, one of the first pronounced and open differences between Eastern and Western Christianity. So...</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/862831-on-the-origin-of-the-dragonblood-exaltation-an-overview-of-an-immaculate-dispute?p=863048#post863048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yes, this one is definitely reminiscent of the old Arian vs Nicean conflict in the early Christian Church during the Roman Empire. Its was over something as simple as 'Is Jesus a creation of God, divine but separate, or is Jesus God in mortal flesh?' People killed over it, and emperors took sides on the issue. The Niceans won out as far as the Catholic and Orthodox are concerned, but the divide hasn't truly disappeared - it's just that fewer people care about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much spot on. Also my main inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1597,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1597-gargulec","user":"Gargulec","date":". 04-10-2016, 06:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1597-gargulec","name":"Gargulec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T05:40:04-07:00","id":863120,"title":"","content":"I'm not arguing that &quot;of vs. from&quot; <i>can't</i> be significant - it's just that its initial presentation itself (and subsequent presentations, for that matter), from what I've gathered, considered it relatively trivial, and that's why it was so extreme that Peleps Deled murdered another monk over it. <br /> <br /> Deled is not supposed to represent your typical Immaculate monk, and while yes, real-world Christians and members of other faiths have killed each other over little differences, it's like Wizard said: there's usually a healthy dose of politics mixed in. <br /> <br /> Deled's not a Nicean, he's the kind of rules-lawyer player who pulls up a Grabowski quote on his laptop and conveniently ignores any rules that would contradict his point, except if the ST continues to disagree or overrule him, Deled breaks his fucking arm. Except usually a rules-lawyer has something to gain aside from the pride-boner of being right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-10-2016, 08:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T06:14:21-07:00","id":863127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/862831-on-the-origin-of-the-dragonblood-exaltation-an-overview-of-an-immaculate-dispute?p=863120#post863120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not arguing that &quot;of vs. from&quot; <i>can't</i> be significant - it's just that its initial presentation itself (and subsequent presentations, for that matter), from what I've gathered, considered it relatively trivial, and that's why it was so extreme that Peleps Deled murdered another monk over it.<br /> <br /> Deled is not supposed to represent your typical Immaculate monk, and while yes, real-world Christians and members of other faiths have killed each other over little differences, it's like Wizard said: there's usually a healthy dose of politics mixed in.<br /> <br /> Deled's not a Nicean, he's the kind of rules-lawyer player who pulls up a Grabowski quote on his laptop and conveniently ignores any rules that would contradict his point, except if the ST continues to disagree or overrule him, Deled breaks his fucking arm. Except usually a rules-lawyer has something to gain aside from the pride-boner of being right.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe there are some misunderstandings between us working here.<br /> <br /> a) Whether this is trivial or not: I have no clue, really. I freely confess that I have not reviewed the relevant material before writing this, and that I have not been all that much &quot;into&quot; Exalted as of couple last years, and only started returning to it recently. Therefore, it possible that what I have written is in clear conflict with the text and the implications contained within books. In that case, the fault is on me for not doing the due research and just expanding on something that was not supposed to be expanded on.<br /> <br /> b) I do not feel like anything within my text suggests that Deled's reaction is typical; having a disagreement about a religious text is one thing, murdering others is another. Deled's reaction is extreme and probably unprecedented, but that does not mean it is something that does not have any sort of roots. Fundamentalist stances also come from somewhere, and I tried to give a genealogy of this particular one. His actions are not representative, not standard and certainly not treated nor accepted as any sort of a norm, even among the more radical-minded Immaculates.<br /> <br /> c) Finally, regarding the healthy dose of politics being mixed into this: I wrote this debate as being over a thousand years old, if not older. Therefore, whatever political contextes that were to it - dependant on the Shogunate politics of that time - are long gone, and as I have tried to imply, the Question of Origination is currently treated as something of an antique curio from the formative times of Immaculate Religion, often derided and ridiculed. That does not mean it is not political, it is just not political in a fresh way.<br /> <br /> While on that point, I would also like to note that while I am very far from denying that such theological disputes are often heavily involved in politics, I would be wary of rendering them to being primarily political or only political. It is a view that easily lapses into an anachronic lack of awareness of a fundamentally different - and more profound - role that theology, with all of its today amusing minutia could and probably have played in the lives of people of different times and cultures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1597-gargulec","name":"Gargulec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T12:54:13-07:00","id":863276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/862831-on-the-origin-of-the-dragonblood-exaltation-an-overview-of-an-immaculate-dispute?p=863120#post863120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deled's not a Nicean, he's the kind of rules-lawyer player who pulls up a Grabowski quote on his laptop and conveniently ignores any rules that would contradict his point, except if the ST continues to disagree or overrule him, Deled breaks his fucking arm. Except usually a rules-lawyer has something to gain aside from the pride-boner of being right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Serious question: how many religious fanatics do you know? I think you may sorely underestimate the <i>size</i> of the pride-boner of being right when it comes to the nature of life, the universe and everything.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T14:39:26-07:00","id":863334,"title":"","content":"You know what's the worst? I find this so cool I was about to just use it as a basis to add some religious intrigue to the Realm Civil War campaign I'm working on, but I'm french, and run games for french players, and I have no idea how to convey the &quot;of the Dragons vs from the Dragons&quot; nuance in our language. In both cases you'd get &quot;des Dragons&quot;.<br /> <br /> That's the worst.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/692-herrtenko","name":"HerrTenko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T14:53:33-07:00","id":863341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerrTenko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/862831-on-the-origin-of-the-dragonblood-exaltation-an-overview-of-an-immaculate-dispute?p=863334#post863334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know what's the worst? I find this so cool I was about to just use it as a basis to add some religious intrigue to the Realm Civil War campaign I'm working on, but I'm french, and run games for french players, and I have no idea how to convey the &quot;of the Dragons vs from the Dragons&quot; nuance in our language. In both cases you'd get &quot;des Dragons&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Try &quot;by the dragons&quot;. If my highschool French serves me right, that's something like:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#212121\">Exalt\u00e9 des dragons contre </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#212121\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Exalt\u00e9 par les dragons ?</span></span></span> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#212121\">l'exaltation n\u00e9e des dragons contre l'exaltation n\u00e9e par les dragons</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#212121\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> ?</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 04-10-2016, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T00:33:51-07:00","id":863514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/862831-on-the-origin-of-the-dragonblood-exaltation-an-overview-of-an-immaculate-dispute?p=863341#post863341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Try &quot;by the dragons&quot;. If my highschool French serves me right, that's something like:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#212121\">Exalt\u00e9 des dragons contre </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#212121\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Exalt\u00e9 par les dragons ?</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#212121\">l'exaltation n\u00e9e des dragons contre l'exaltation n\u00e9e par les dragons</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#212121\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> ?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually that seems like a very obvious solution now that you mention it. Many thanks, now I get to add religious strife to the list of stuff my players will have to contend with!<br /> <br /> This Civil War campaign is looking more and more like a Game of Thrones Season...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/692-herrtenko","name":"HerrTenko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T15:46:57-07:00","id":863944,"title":"","content":"So, I've decided to write something more on various interesting stories about weird heretical nonsense from Creation's past, in a semi-similar style. Hope you like it! Since it contains footnotes, and the text editor of this forum seems to be a wretched, nightmarish thing, I'll link to it instead of posting it straight.<br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Heresies of Kanyu Gusei:</b></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VVMR41tLKwC_EGwc8qTKAeXzNQxiR8WQ5tSYyicBQvQ/edit\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VVMR41tLKwC_EGwc8qTKAeXzNQxiR8WQ5tSYyicBQvQ</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1597,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1597-gargulec","user":"Gargulec","date":".  what the hell is this text editor, it is evil 04-11-2016, 06:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1597-gargulec","name":"Gargulec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T17:02:56-07:00","id":863970,"title":"","content":"I get that in its original context, the whole &quot;of vs from&quot; things feels like a kind of punchline to the whole theological duel to the death thing, and that was probably the intent. Yet, when I read about the actual dispute between Western and Eastern Christianity concerning whether or not the term &quot;and the Son&quot; should be added to prayers addressing the emergence of the Holy Spirit, well, it can't help but feel sufficiently real to me to be afforded a measure of seriousness. I still don't think this needs to detract from Deled, since I don't think there's really any issue in the Order for which it would be considered acceptable to duel to the death (or at least not with such an unnecessarily brutal finishing move). I might even say that focusing too much on the idea of him doing it over trivialities and minutia is something that verges on caricature, at least retroactively (by which I mean, not bad at the time, but maybe refine it a bit).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T17:06:42-07:00","id":863971,"title":"","content":"These are fantastic. Always nice to see a fan with a scholarly bent churning out high-quality fiction. Gusei's piece was perfectly written and had real tonal changes for the quoted portions. It sounded very authentic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}